{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Let it come</b> — because Israel in exile is like a prisoner in a dungeon." "<b>The groaning</b> — from the root of הותירם, meaning those who are ready to die; its pattern is like תמותה, תשועה, תקומה, תרועה. And Rabbi Moses [ibn Janah] said: הותר means to remove the peg and open their bonds, because he mentioned prisoner."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 79, :notes {1 "Resolved the single root letter reference as הותירם (the form Ibn Ezra cites to illustrate the root); רבי משה resolved as Ibn Janah by inference from his role as a grammatical authority frequently cited under this epithet."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:30.405741154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}